{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Performance"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","text":"The binary-size budget","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CI builds ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"text":" on every push and sums the resulting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"text":" sizes for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"text":" each store their running ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" in a private ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"text":" property, read by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":". Every one of those ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":"s captures ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In practice, a completed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"running","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" operation: without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","type":"reference"},{"text":" for the rest of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":" safety net this guarantee supports.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","type":"reference"},{"text":" only ever go active once ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" have confirmed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"text":" is already ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" — both fall back to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)